Desktop/

# Secrets kept as loose notes.
#
# A password file was saved into this folder on 11 Oct 2026 and would have
# been committed to a PUBLIC repository by the next `git add -A`. These
# patterns stop that happening again, case-insensitively and whatever the
# extension. They are a safety net, not a filing system: a secret is safer
# outside the repository altogether.
*[Pp]assword*
*[Pp]asswords*
*[Pp]aasword*
*[Ss]ecret*
*[Cc]redential*
*.key
*.pem
